From 0e5ddb05a625b03934eaa7deb3bfd5dc4608a67c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:32:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] input: add the selection primitives that a Vim keymap needs

A Vim keymap for the copy mode of an embedder needs three things that
the Helix primitives of patch 0013 do not give:

  move_selection:next_word_start   Vim `w`: the first cell of the next
                                   word, not the cell before it
  select_line_bounds               Vim `V`, Helix `X`: whole rows, with
                                   the direction kept, no growth
  selection_rectangle:on|off       Vim `Ctrl-v`: the block selection

select_line_bounds keeps each end the anchor or the head that it was,
so a motion of the head after it still moves the same end. select_line
(Helix `x`) normalizes the direction and grows by a row, which is right
for Helix and wrong for a Vim `Vk`.

Selection.expandToLineBounds and nextWordStart are tested in
Selection.zig.
---
